const PRIVACY = "## Introduction\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how Gonzalo Cifuentes (\"we\", \"us\", or \"our\") processes information in connection with the mobile application (the \"App\"). It describes the information processed on your device, the limited information shared with service providers, and your choices and rights.\n\nThe App allows you to connect and manage compatible home cameras, view available camera feeds and events, save media to your Photos library, and use a text-based AI assistant.\n\n## Data Controller and Contact\n\nFor the processing described in this Privacy Policy, the data controller is Gonzalo Cifuentes, Calle Martínez Maldonado 91, Málaga, Spain. For privacy inquiries, contact gonzaloit@cifuentes.store.\n\n## Information Processed by the App\n\nCamera and Home information. Depending on the connected device and available permissions, the App processes camera connection details, device capabilities and settings, available battery information, live video, recorded events, and motion, person, or animal detection information. This information is accessed and handled through supported HomeKit functionality. The App does not upload camera video, camera recordings, or detected event media to servers operated by us.\n\nInformation stored on the device. The App may store camera configuration, preferences, activity history, local profile or sign-in information, and AI conversation history on your device. Local account-related information is not maintained on an account server operated by us.\n\nAI assistant content. When you use the AI assistant, your text messages and relevant conversation history are transmitted to OpenAI to generate a response. The request may also contain system instructions needed to operate the assistant. Images, video, and recordings from your cameras are not sent to OpenAI by this feature.\n\nSubscription information. To activate and manage paid features, subscription status and related purchase information are processed through Apple in-app purchases and Apphud. Apphud may process technical or SDK-generated identifiers needed to associate subscription transactions with the App and provide entitlement status.\n\nAttribution and permission information. The App may use Apple-provided attribution features to understand app acquisition and may display an App Tracking Transparency (ATT) request. If tracking permission is requested, you can allow or deny it through iOS settings.\n\n## Device Permissions\n\n- HomeKit: to discover, connect to, and manage supported home camera accessories and available functionality.\n- Camera: to scan QR codes when adding or configuring supported devices.\n- Photos (Add Only): to save images or recordings to your device’s Photos library at your request.\n- Local notifications: to present notifications generated on your device. The App does not use remote push notifications.\n- App Tracking Transparency: the App may ask for permission when required for permitted attribution or tracking-related functionality. You can manage this choice in iOS settings.\n\nYou can manage applicable permissions in your device settings. Denying a permission may limit the feature that depends on it.\n\n## AI Assistant and OpenAI\n\nThe AI assistant uses services provided by OpenAI. When you submit a request, the App sends the text of your request, relevant previous messages in the conversation, and necessary system instructions to OpenAI so that a response can be generated.\n\nPlease avoid entering personal, confidential, or sensitive information that is not needed for your request. OpenAI processes information it receives in order to provide the AI service, subject to its applicable terms and privacy practices. The App stores its own conversation history locally on your device unless you delete it.\n\n## Subscriptions and Apphud\n\nPaid subscriptions are billed by Apple through the App Store. Apphud is used to verify and manage subscription entitlements. For this purpose, Apphud may receive subscription transaction details, purchase status, and limited device or SDK identifiers required for subscription operation.\n\nWe do not use Apphud as a separate advertising platform. Purchase records may also be maintained by Apple and applicable service providers according to their own obligations and retention practices.\n\n## Attribution and Advertising\n\nThe App does not display third-party advertising. Apple advertising attribution functionality may be used to understand how installations are attributed to acquisition campaigns. The App may display an ATT permission request. If you deny tracking permission, the App will not access the advertising identifier (IDFA) for tracking without your permission.\n\nThe availability of attribution data and related controls depends on iOS and Apple services. A permission request, by itself, does not mean that camera data or AI chats are used for advertising.\n\n## How Information Is Shared\n\nWe share information only as needed to provide the features described above: with OpenAI for AI text processing; with Apphud for subscription verification and management; and through Apple services for in-app purchases, HomeKit functionality, device permissions, and supported attribution.\n\nWe do not sell your personal information. We do not operate a separate service that stores users’ camera video or recordings. Data processed by Apple, OpenAI, or Apphud may be subject to those providers’ own applicable privacy terms.\n\n## Storage, Retention, and Deletion\n\nApp settings, local account information, activity history, and AI conversation history are generally stored on your device. You can delete available local chats, logs, and settings using the App’s controls. Settings → Delete Account removes the locally maintained account information associated with the App.\n\nPhotos or recordings saved to your Photos library remain under your control and must be deleted separately in Photos if you no longer want to keep them.\n\nDeleting local data does not automatically remove records independently maintained by Apple or service providers, such as Apple purchase records or subscription transaction records retained for operational or legal reasons. Retention by OpenAI and Apphud is governed by their applicable practices and requirements.\n\n## Legal Bases and International Processing\n\nWhere the GDPR or similar privacy laws apply, we process information as necessary to provide the features you request and fulfill our obligations to you; to comply with legal obligations; and, where required, on the basis of your consent, including device-level permissions. Limited processing may also be based on legitimate interests such as maintaining subscription functionality and preventing misuse, where permitted by law.\n\nOpenAI, Apphud, or Apple may process certain information outside your country. Where international transfer rules apply, such transfers must be supported by appropriate legal mechanisms and safeguards.\n\n## Security\n\nWe take reasonable measures appropriate to the operation of the App to protect information under our control. Device-level protection also depends on your iOS security settings, device access controls, and Apple services. No system can guarantee absolute security.\n\n## Your Privacy Rights\n\nDepending on applicable law, you may have rights to request access to, correction of, deletion of, or restriction of personal data; object to certain processing; request portability; and withdraw consent where processing is based on consent. You may also lodge a complaint with a competent data protection authority, including the Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD) where applicable.\n\nFor information stored only on your device, these rights can often be exercised directly using the App or device controls. For requests relating to processing under our control, contact gonzaloit@cifuentes.store. Requests concerning data held independently by Apple or other providers may need to be directed to the relevant provider.\n\n## Children’s Privacy\n\nThe App is not designed to collect personal information from children independently of their parent or guardian. Users are responsible for ensuring that camera placement, recording, and access comply with applicable laws, including protections for children.\n\n## Changes to This Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes to the App, its services, or applicable requirements. The updated version will be made available through the App or another appropriate channel. Material changes will be communicated where required by law.\n\n## Contact\n\nGonzalo Cifuentes\nCalle Martínez Maldonado 91, Málaga, Spain\nEmail: gonzaloit@cifuentes.store";

const TERMS = "## Agreement to These Terms\n\nThese Terms of Use (\"Terms\") govern access to and use of the mobile application (the \"App\") provided by Gonzalo Cifuentes (\"we\", \"us\", or \"our\"). By using the App, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the App.\n\nYou must comply with applicable laws and the terms that govern your device, the App Store, and any connected equipment or services.\n\n## What the App Provides\n\nThe App offers features for setup and management of compatible home camera accessories, including supported QR-based setup, Wi-Fi configuration guidance, live camera viewing, review of available recorded events, camera detection controls, saving selected media to Photos, and a text-based AI assistant.\n\nThe availability of any feature depends on the camera model, device capabilities, software versions, network conditions, HomeKit support, and permissions. We do not guarantee compatibility with every camera or that all advertised functions are available for all devices.\n\n## Device Access and Permissions\n\nYou are responsible for obtaining permission to connect to, operate, and view any camera or property monitored through the App. Use of the App may require access to HomeKit, your device camera for QR scanning, Photos for saving media, or local notifications.\n\nYou are responsible for providing a functioning network connection, keeping supported equipment configured appropriately, and protecting access to your phone and connected cameras. Revoking a device permission may prevent certain functions from operating.\n\n## Local Profiles and Account Access\n\nThe App may provide local profile, registration, or sign-in functionality to support access to available features. Where provided, this information is maintained on the device rather than through a separate account service operated by us.\n\nYou are responsible for keeping your access credentials and device secure. Local account information may be removed through Settings → Delete Account. Deleting a local profile does not necessarily cancel an active App Store subscription.\n\n## Subscriptions and Purchases\n\nThe App may offer optional paid subscriptions that unlock certain features or content. The price, billing period, and features of each offer are displayed in the App Store purchase interface before you confirm a purchase.\n\nSubscriptions are charged to your Apple Account and generally renew automatically unless canceled in accordance with Apple’s applicable subscription rules. You can manage or cancel a subscription in your Apple Account subscription settings. Deleting the App or a local account does not automatically cancel a subscription.\n\nPayment processing, billing history, cancellations, and refunds are administered by Apple under its applicable terms and mandatory consumer protections. Apphud is used to recognize and manage subscription status within the App. If available, the App may offer a restore-purchases option.\n\n## AI Assistant\n\nThe App may provide an AI-powered assistant for general information about camera setup, connectivity, and related usage questions. User-entered text, relevant conversation history, and necessary instructions are processed by OpenAI to generate responses.\n\nAI responses can be inaccurate, incomplete, or unsuitable for your particular device. You should verify important instructions against the documentation and security guidance for your camera and operating system. The AI assistant is not a substitute for professional installation, security advice, or emergency assistance.\n\nDo not submit unlawful content or information you are not authorized to disclose, and avoid including unnecessary sensitive information in AI messages.\n\n## Camera Data and Responsible Use\n\nYou must use camera viewing, recording, and detection features lawfully. You are solely responsible for obtaining any notices, permissions, or consents required before recording or monitoring people or spaces, and for complying with applicable privacy, surveillance, and data protection laws.\n\nThe App processes available camera feeds and events using compatible device and HomeKit functionality. You are responsible for managing recordings and images saved to your device, including content exported to the Photos library.\n\nThe App is not an emergency response service or a guaranteed professional security monitoring solution. Detection, notifications, playback, and connectivity may be delayed, unavailable, or inaccurate, including because of network conditions, hardware limitations, or third-party services.\n\n## Acceptable Use\n\nYou agree not to use the App to violate law or the rights of others; access cameras or networks without authorization; invade privacy; interfere with device or network security; or attempt to reverse engineer, disrupt, or abuse App functionality except where applicable law expressly permits.\n\nWe may limit access to features when reasonably necessary to protect the App, users, or legal compliance, subject to applicable consumer rights.\n\n## Intellectual Property and Trademarks\n\nThe App and its original software, interface, and content are protected by applicable intellectual property laws. Subject to these Terms, you receive a limited, personal, non-transferable right to use the App for its intended purposes.\n\nYI and YI Home trademarks and related brand assets are used under authorization. Those marks remain the property of their respective rights holder. Apple, HomeKit, and other names or marks are the property of their respective owners. Nothing in these Terms transfers ownership of any trademark or other intellectual property to you.\n\n## Availability and Third-Party Services\n\nCertain features depend on Apple services, HomeKit, supported camera hardware, OpenAI, and subscription infrastructure. These services may have their own terms, privacy notices, operational limitations, or availability requirements.\n\nWe may make changes reasonably necessary to maintain functionality, compatibility, security, or legal compliance. We do not promise uninterrupted operation or permanent availability of every feature.\n\n## Privacy\n\nOur Privacy Policy explains how information is handled in connection with the App, including local device storage, AI text processing through OpenAI, subscription processing through Apphud, and Apple services. Please review it alongside these Terms.\n\n## Disclaimers and Liability\n\nTo the extent permitted by applicable law, the App is provided on an \"as available\" basis. We do not guarantee that camera connections, recording, detection, notifications, AI-generated text, or supported integrations will always be accurate, secure, uninterrupted, or error-free.\n\nNothing in these Terms excludes or limits liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, nor does it affect any mandatory rights you have as a consumer under applicable law. Subject to those rights, we are not responsible for losses caused by unauthorized device access, user misconfiguration, network failures, unsupported equipment, or third-party outages beyond our reasonable control.\n\n## Ending Use\n\nYou may stop using the App at any time. You may remove local account information using Settings → Delete Account and uninstall the App. Media saved in Photos must be deleted separately if you no longer wish to keep it.\n\nTerminating use of the App does not itself terminate an Apple subscription; you must cancel it through Apple’s subscription-management controls. Provisions that by their nature should survive termination, including intellectual property and applicable liability provisions, will continue to apply.\n\n## Changes to These Terms\n\nWe may update these Terms as required to reflect product, legal, or operational changes. Updated Terms will be made available through the App or another appropriate channel. Where applicable law requires notice or consent, we will provide it.\n\n## Governing Law\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of Spain, except where mandatory consumer protection rules in your country of residence provide otherwise. Nothing in these Terms limits your right to bring a claim before a court or authority that has jurisdiction under applicable consumer law.\n\n## Contact\n\nGonzalo Cifuentes\nCalle Martínez Maldonado 91, Málaga, Spain\nEmail: gonzaloit@cifuentes.store";

